From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mfreadwrite: Stop retaining delivered audio samples.

The Source Reader changes in the media rework keep an extra reference to
every delivered audio sample until a flush, seek, or stream destruction.
Clients which correctly release samples after copying their data still
accumulate decoded buffers for the entire playback interval.

Both logs in #795 show allocation failures in the 32-bit Apple Jack process
before FNA's MOJOSHADER_compileEffect reports out-of-memory. The game plays
music through the Source Reader, and FAudio releases the samples it reads.
Unbounded reader-side retention is a likely cause of this failure.

Remove the delivered-audio history. Both read-result paths already acquire
the caller's reference before releasing the queued response, so no extra
retention is needed to keep the returned sample alive. Preserve queued
samples, transform draining, and timestamp handling.

Add ownership checks for both FIRST_AUDIO_STREAM and ANY_STREAM using the
existing PCM test source. Read subsequent samples before checking that an
earlier sample has only the caller's reference, without flushing or seeking
(which would hide the leak).

References:
https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/795
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/mfreadwrite/nf-mfreadwrite-imfsourcereader-readsample

Rebased 2026-10-30: drop reader.c hunks (already upstream).
---
diff --git a/dlls/mfreadwrite/tests/mfplat.c b/dlls/mfreadwrite/tests/mfplat.c
--- a/dlls/mfreadwrite/tests/mfplat.c
+++ b/dlls/mfreadwrite/tests/mfplat.c
@@ -1154,6 +1154,44 @@
     winetest_pop_context();
 }
 
+static void check_source_reader_sample_lifetime(IMFSourceReader *reader, DWORD stream_index)
+{
+    IMFSample *first_sample = NULL, *sample;
+    DWORD actual_index, stream_flags;
+    LONGLONG timestamp;
+    unsigned int i;
+    ULONG refcount;
+    HRESULT hr;
+
+    winetest_push_context("stream %#lx", stream_index);
+
+    /* Read past the first sample so its delivery callback can finish, without
+     * flushing or seeking away any references retained by the reader. */
+    for (i = 0; i < 32; ++i)
+    {
+        sample = NULL;
+        hr = IMFSourceReader_ReadSample(reader, stream_index, 0, &actual_index, &stream_flags,
+                &timestamp, &sample);
+        ok(hr == S_OK, "Unexpected hr %#lx.\n", hr);
+        ok(!!sample, "Expected sample object.\n");
+        if (!sample) break;
+
+        if (!first_sample)
+            first_sample = sample;
+        else
+            IMFSample_Release(sample);
+    }
+
+    if (first_sample)
+    {
+        refcount = get_refcount(first_sample);
+        ok(refcount == 1, "Expected only the caller's sample reference, got %lu.\n", refcount);
+        IMFSample_Release(first_sample);
+    }
+
+    winetest_pop_context();
+}
+
 static void test_source_reader_from_media_source(void)
 {
     static const DWORD expected_sample_order[10] = {0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0};
@@ -1303,6 +1341,9 @@
     ok(!!sample, "Expected sample object.\n");
     IMFSample_Release(sample);
 
+    check_source_reader_sample_lifetime(reader, MF_SOURCE_READER_FIRST_AUDIO_STREAM);
+    check_source_reader_sample_lifetime(reader, MF_SOURCE_READER_ANY_STREAM);
+
     IMFSourceReader_Release(reader);
     IMFMediaSource_Release(source);
 
